  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ai Hub for Sustainable Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Artificial Intelligence Hub for Sustainable Development (AI Hub) is a flagship initiative of the Italian Ministry of Enterprises and Made in Italy (MIMIT) and the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), created under Italy&#x2019;s Mattei Plan to drive AI-powered industrial growth in Africa. Headquartered in Rome, the Hub connects African innovators, start-ups, and private sector actors with companies and institutions from Italy, the EU, and the G7 to strengthen critical AI foundations &#x2014; including compute infrastructure, data ecosystems, talent development, and responsible investment. Through accelerator programmes, strategic partnerships, and investment pipelines, it aims to enable large-scale AI adoption in priority sectors such as energy, agriculture, healthcare, education, and infrastructure, fostering inclusive, sustainable development and equitable global collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
